---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../../components/Newsletter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Feedback and support — Collectively Bzy" description="Feedback and support information for Collectively Bzy projects.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Feedback + support</div><h1>Tell us where it catches.</h1><p>Found a rough edge, have a thoughtful suggestion, or need a hand with one of our projects? This is where the support path will live.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split-callout"><div class="split-callout-art" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="split-callout-copy"><div class="eyebrow">A clear path</div><h2>Support details are coming soon.</h2><p>The first release keeps this page ready for a support email, FAQs, app-specific help, and feedback links without collecting unnecessary visitor data.</p><a class="button" href="/">Return home</a></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section sand"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Feedback</div><h2>Bring the useful details.</h2></div><p>When the support channel is connected, this section can hold app-specific help, feedback instructions, and a clear way to report a problem without exposing private infrastructure.</p></div><div class="grid three"><article class="card"><div><div class="eyebrow">Apps</div><h3 class="card-title">Something not working?</h3><p class="card-copy">Choose the app, note what happened, and include the device or browser details that help us reproduce it.</p></div></article><article class="card"><div><div class="eyebrow">Store</div><h3 class="card-title">Have a product note?</h3><p class="card-copy">A future store feedback path can route product questions and special-related comments to the right team.</p></div></article><article class="card"><div><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h3 class="card-title">Keep it lightweight.</h3><p class="card-copy">The site will collect only what a chosen support or newsletter provider needs, with no unnecessary tracking.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
  <Newsletter />
</BaseLayout>
